ts=2026-02-19T20:20:32.358Z type=context scope=Obscura_Chat_Architecture content="Chat/Room Feature Architecture Exploration Complete

TWO IMPLEMENTATIONS EXIST:
1. Chat Feature (NEW/ACTIVE) - Sequelize/Express pattern with Message entity, used for real chat
2. Room Feature (LEGACY/DEPRECATED) - TypeORM/Elysia pattern, entity files are empty

KEY ENTITIES:
- Connection: Two-way user connection, tracks message_count and reveal status
- Message: Individual chat messages tied to connections
- User, Profile: Referenced by connection/message

KEY BUSINESS LOGIC:
- Message threshold of 50 triggers connection.status = \"REVEAL_READY\"
- Both users must vote to reveal identities
- Connections can be soft-deleted
- Messages ordered oldest-first when retrieved

ENDPOINTS (Chat):
- POST /chat/message (send message, increments count in transaction)
- GET /chat/:connectionId (get all messages for connection)

SUPPORTING ENDPOINTS (Connection):
- POST /connections (create connection)
- GET /connections (list user's connections)
- POST /connections/:id/reveal-vote (vote to reveal)
- DELETE /connections/:id (soft delete)

CURRENT ISSUES:
1. Mixed framework architecture (Elysia + Express + TypeORM + Sequelize)
2. Empty entity files (room.entity.ts, message.entity.ts)
3. Message model not in database.ts DBModels
4. Chat service still uses TypeORM/DataSource patterns
5. No comprehensive WebSocket integration

MIGRATION PATTERN TO FOLLOW:
- Use Connection feature as model (Express/Sequelize setup)
- Use Question feature as secondary pattern reference
- Create Message entity with Sequelize
- Migrate all to Express + Sequelize transactions
- Deprecate Room feature entirely

See CHAT_ARCHITECTURE.md for complete 14-section architecture overview" tags=chat,room,architecture,entities,endpoints,migration
